From dbd2d32bd935b8b271141667e41546c904e74e8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ephico2real2 <ephico2real@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:17:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ztunnel/xds: verify all retained node bindings before
 publishing

A later Address batch for an unchanged node replaced the node-table watch
without re-verifying earlier bindings. A node change that had already closed
the previous watch could then be hidden, leaving a workload published under a
stale node name (primary and Cursor Grok review finding).

Track published bindings by immutable Pod UID. Each batch stages the complete
retained set (previous bindings minus REMOVED UIDs plus the new batch) and
verifies all of it in one node-table read; the watch comes from that same
read. Re-verify immediately before SendMsg and commit only after a successful
send. A rejected batch, a change during conversion or a failed send leaves the
published set and the closed watch unchanged, so the stream still ends.
Removing one Pod keeps the dependency of another Pod on the same node; the
last removal retires it so address reuse under a new name succeeds.

Tests: the reviewer's reproduction fails on the previous commit (stale batch
accepted) and the equivalent test passes now; new send-time withholding,
exact-UID retirement and failed-send tests. pkg/ztunnel/xds race 67 top-level
/ 169 total pass, vet clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: ephico2real2 <ephico2real@gmail.com>
